claimed: okay-script-application -- JSP's `application` scope for a Site, and the second worked example built on it. api.Application: attributes shared by EVERY page of a Site (String values, plus Schema-typed get/set as JSON), engines memory / persisted(store) over a keyed compacted topic like Sessions; Site(application = ...). api.signIn(subject, scopes): the container mints the token with Site(issue = Some((subject, scopes) => token)) beside verify, so a login page never holds an issuer of its own. Example: examples/site gains login.md (password + signIn), admin.md (secure: admin, Live.form[Product] into Application) and index.md reading the catalog from Application. Touches Api.scala (+Application.scala), Site.scala, specs, the example, TestSiteExample.
